Hi Sudhir,

Thanks for sharing your results. In my opinion you got an amazing result 148 in 150.

It happens because sometime two plants are too close and touching each other and the algorithm doesn't recognize as two different objects. Also, when you use minSize=0.8 you are eliminating the really small plant in your second line (maybe you should to use 0.7 or 0.5 and see if it can control this problem)

FIELDimageR uses image segmentation approaches. The quality of your analysis will depends of your image quality (for example, taking pictures in early stages and avoiding plants touching each other).

Another solution is to try play around with the fieldMask (changing indices) and chose another index to help you split better your plants.

Let me know if you fixed it, but again your results are impressive due to evaluating late plants (touching each other).

Best,
Filipe Matias

